    "body": "ROME — Italian defense giant Leonardo has rolled out the first of 15 M-346 jets due to take over stunt flying duties with the Italian Air Force’s aerobatic team.\nBuilt as a jet trainer and also sold in a light fighter configuration, the M-346 jets configured for display team flying will be delivered to the Frecce Tricolori team between 2027 and 2028, Leonardo said in a statement.\nThe aircraft will replace the MB-339 PAN aircraft which has flown for more than 40 years, allowing for better aerobatic displays thanks to the M-346’s greater maneuverability, Leonardo said.\n“The M-346 is now well positioned to pursue major new commercial and industrial cooperation opportunities worldwide, both as a trainer and multirole aircraft and as a platform for aerobatic teams,” said Stefano Bortoli, managing director of Leonardo’s Aircraft Division.\nThe new jets will be upgraded for the job with a smoke generation system, video streaming capabilities, avionics modifications and auxiliary fuel tanks.\nLeonardo has now sold over 170 M-346 jets to 10 countries, with Italy, the Republic of Singapore, Israel, Poland, Qatar and Greece among customers for the trainer version.\nThe light fighter version has been sold to Turkmenistan, Nigeria, Austria and most recently Indonesia.\nThe M-346 F “Block 20” light fighter configuration comes with a Large Area Display (LAD), active electronically scanned radar, a Link 16 data-link, electronic countermeasures, and new weapons systems.",
